Async totals come back as zero. Save /workspace/enrich.mjs:

export async function totalSpend(userIds, lookupSpend) {
  let total = 0;
  userIds.forEach(async (id) => {
    const spend = await lookupSpend(id);
    total += spend;
  });
  return total;
}

forEach ignores the promises returned by an async callback, so totalSpend returns before any lookup resolves. Write enrich.test.mjs (node:test) first: lookupSpend resolves id * 10 after setTimeout 5ms; totalSpend([1, 2, 3], lookupSpend) must resolve to 60; run node --test and watch it return 0. Fix with Promise.all over map (keep lookups concurrent; add a test that 50 lookups of 20ms each complete in well under 500ms total to prove you did not serialize them). Also handle a rejecting lookup: totalSpend must reject. All green.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

